    "normalization_course_correction": {
      "receipt_kind": "current_user_course_correction_before_launch",
      "source_thread_id": "01a034b9-a1c8-7a80-937f-4e45e3f2ae45",
      "text_sha256": "cebc005f707144a0efe7c33ae54b0971e43ef6039f3416814fc41b85928ce184",
      "text_utf8": "USER COURSE CORRECTION BEFORE LAUNCH: response normalization must accept semantically equivalent model variation. Do NOT require input JSON object insertion/key order. Interpret objective's `schema/type/value/order` as strict schema/types/values, meaningful list/sequence order, and deterministic schema-defined order in the emitted canonical minified result. Accept different surrounding prose, whitespace, PM_RESULT location, and object-key order. Still reject malformed JSON, duplicate keys, nonfinite values, missing/extra fields, wrong types/values, reordered meaningful arrays, zero candidates, and conflicting non-identical candidates; no repair/coercion/invention. Multiple candidates may differ only in benign formatting/object-key order and must canonicalize to the same typed semantic value. Keep lifecycle/tool/retry/exit gates strict. Update package/normalizer/selftests/contract accordingly before launch; do not use byte-identical V6 order-sensitive normalizer.",
      "text_utf8_bytes": 976
    },
    "normalization_program_authority": {
      "assistant_contract": {
        "jsonl_line_bytes_including_lf": 1093,
        "jsonl_line_sha256_including_lf": "cada218ad7952e36572e7dcb297f30e28d4a4cc0c9b7cff4284b268dad9cc351",
        "message_id": "msg_09747b8db7972cfa016a8f5ae67af887d1abb585a8a8783f7e",
        "ordinal": 28926,
        "phase": "commentary",
        "physical_line": 28927,
        "role": "assistant",
        "text_sha256": "00bbefdf07b901f3665bb3c27e778bb53f325bc48095ce2f6cb678787e7a2acd",
        "text_utf8": "Agreed. The harness-specific final prose is not a stable product contract, so requiring byte-exact terminal prose is the wrong invariant.\n\nThe stable contract should be:\n\n- native Goal must activate and complete;\n- the model must emit one schema-valid typed result somewhere in the bounded task lifecycle;\n- the host deterministically extracts, validates, and canonicalizes that result;\n- conflicting multiple results fail;\n- surrounding prose and harness-specific final wording are ignored.\n\nThat keeps semantics, authority, and lifecycle strict while making the output portable to PuppetMaster’s eventual native runtime. I’ll pivot the qualification to a fresh normalized-output denominator; no old failure gets retro-credit.",
        "text_utf8_bytes": 731,
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T21:30:18.154Z",
        "turn_id": "01a03f9b-da82-7a93-b8c7-6974cc7f563d"
      },
      "assistant_program_answer": {
        "jsonl_line_bytes_including_lf": 958,
        "jsonl_line_sha256_including_lf": "eaefd3b7971cc283d72b11125803ccab28464e9e133751fe8b8904f428b5243d",
        "message_id": "msg_09747b8db7972cfa016a8f5b7cb43887d19b351f7f6ca3612e",
        "ordinal": 28946,
        "phase": "final_answer",
        "physical_line": 28947,
        "role": "assistant",
        "text_sha256": "e9c484ce848b0aa2638ac3bf11250d6bdc2490f6770371b8860dd8bf379e3e44",
        "text_utf8": "A program, not another agent.\n\nThe PuppetMaster host/controller would:\n\n1. Read the bounded task’s raw assistant outputs.\n2. Extract every `PM_RESULT` candidate.\n3. Strictly parse and schema-validate them.\n4. Require all valid candidates to represent the same typed value.\n5. Reject missing, malformed, or conflicting results.\n6. Emit one canonical minified JSON result.\n\nNo model call or judgment is involved. For qualification, the program also compares that canonical result with the frozen oracle. This keeps normalization deterministic, cheap, and independent of harness-specific prose.",
        "text_utf8_bytes": 593,
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T21:32:47.399Z",
        "turn_id": "01a03f9b-da82-7a93-b8c7-6974cc7f563d"
      },
      "source_jsonl_basename": "rollout-2026-08-24T17-02-55-01a034b9-a1c8-7a80-937f-4e45e3f2ae45.jsonl",
      "user_correction": {
        "jsonl_line_bytes_including_lf": 565,
        "jsonl_line_sha256_including_lf": "36969d325f589bc533babc46dd38c32437a45195602e40afa0b034b210eec97c",
        "message_id": "msg_01a03ffa-f335-71b0-bca2-c69f0727786c",
        "ordinal": 28921,
        "phase": null,
        "physical_line": 28922,
        "role": "user",
        "text_sha256": "00e40f2fb20461d8714a37cc5380fa126312621ca6ce5efed9c540c9920b426e",
        "text_utf8": "Keep in mind, the harness the ai agent is using will change responses slightly, so running natively in Puppet Master, once built, will give a slightly different prose response.  So the only option is likely normalizing.\n",
        "text_utf8_bytes": 220,
        "timestamp": "2026-08-26T21:30:06.005Z",
        "turn_id": "01a03f9b-da82-7a93-b8c7-6974cc7f563d"
      },
      "user_host_question": {
        "jsonl_line_bytes_including_lf": 481,
        "jsonl_line_sha256_including_lf": "0dab2444dc8e8ba9c7ccc62bcf8f6fcf1446f9695c7c42aa9696d6e394a1cdf1",
        "message_id": "msg_01a03ffd-2b73-7051-9c8d-3872550c5304",
